WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.234
It is so great to see you again.

00:00:02.234 --> 00:00:03.667
-Gosh, it's so great to --
I'm sorry about that

00:00:03.667 --> 00:00:04.901
whole sitting fiasco.

00:00:04.901 --> 00:00:06.000
It's been a while since I was
on a talk show.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.634
-"No, you hang up."
"No, you hang up."

00:00:07.634 --> 00:00:10.000
Yeah, exactly.
-"You hang up."

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:13.334
-I want to talk to you about
"Joe vs. Carole."

00:00:13.334 --> 00:00:15.067
Great job, by the way.
-Wow. Thanks.

00:00:15.067 --> 00:00:16.200
-And I really do --
I want to talk about that

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:17.300
and how you got into it.

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:19.000
-And we will, you know.
-And we will.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:21.100
But, first,
"Saturday Night Live."

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:22.534
-Yeah.
-You just crush it.

00:00:22.534 --> 00:00:24.868
I love seeing you on there,
and I go,

00:00:24.868 --> 00:00:26.133
"How many years has
Kate been on?"

00:00:26.133 --> 00:00:28.434
I go, "Five years?"

00:00:28.434 --> 00:00:29.767
You've been on
for almost 10 years.

00:00:29.767 --> 00:00:33.734
-It's been 10 years, which is --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:33.734 --> 00:00:36.100
-It doesn't feel like -- Does it
feel like 10 years to you?

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:38.133
-It feels like a day.

00:00:38.133 --> 00:00:41.100
It feels like
ten-hundred-thousand

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:42.801
billion years.

00:00:42.801 --> 00:00:45.067
I don't remember the beforetime.

00:00:45.067 --> 00:00:48.267
I only remember
the last 10 years,

00:00:48.267 --> 00:00:51.868
and, like, it's changed
my concept of time.

00:00:51.868 --> 00:00:54.033
Like, I no longer think of
Tuesday as, like, Tuesday.

00:00:54.033 --> 00:00:55.033
I think of it as, like,
writing night.

00:00:55.033 --> 00:00:57.067
-Writing night. Yeah.
-And...

00:00:57.067 --> 00:00:59.000
-Me too.
-Yeah. Still?

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:00.067
-Yeah.
-Oh, boy.

00:01:00.067 --> 00:01:01.834
-Tuesdays, yeah,
I teach my kids.

00:01:01.834 --> 00:01:03.100
I teach my kids.

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:05.434
It does stick in your head.
-It's a good system.

00:01:05.434 --> 00:01:07.968
-Yeah. That's "SNL" stuff, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:07.968 --> 00:01:09.200
-Well, congrats on 10 years.

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:10.701
I can't believe
it's been almost 10 years.

00:01:10.701 --> 00:01:11.934
You're fantastic.
-Thank you.

00:01:11.934 --> 00:01:14.100
[ Cheers and applause ]
Thanks.

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:16.133
-Oh, you know,
I also want to bring up

00:01:16.133 --> 00:01:18.567
you're going to be in
the new "Barbie" movie.

00:01:18.567 --> 00:01:20.367
-"Barbie" movie!

00:01:20.367 --> 00:01:21.968
-No, you are,
with Margot Robbie.

00:01:21.968 --> 00:01:23.100
This is --
-I know!

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:24.567
-Greta Gerwig.
-Can you even believe?

00:01:24.567 --> 00:01:26.100
-Directing!
-Directing!

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:28.934
Yes. Ryan Gosling -- Ken!

00:01:28.934 --> 00:01:30.868
-Yes, I know!
-Ken and Barbie!

00:01:30.868 --> 00:01:33.634
-This is a big -- Aah!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:33.634 --> 00:01:36.534
Greta Gerwig. "Barbie" movie.
I can't believe it.

00:01:36.534 --> 00:01:38.834
I can't believe my good fortune.
-No, seriously.

00:01:38.834 --> 00:01:41.133
What is -- Do you know Greta
at all, Greta Gerwig?

00:01:41.133 --> 00:01:43.634
-I went to college with
Greta, yeah.

00:01:43.634 --> 00:01:47.901
We lived in the same
disgusting dorm suite.

00:01:47.901 --> 00:01:50.968
I mean, a dorm suite so filthy,

00:01:50.968 --> 00:01:54.467
a dorm suite
with vomit in the tub

00:01:54.467 --> 00:01:57.100
that you -- You don't know
where it came from.

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:58.367
-Just something got sick
in your tub.

00:01:58.367 --> 00:02:00.367
-And you don't know
who's going to clean it up,

00:02:00.367 --> 00:02:02.167
and no one does.

00:02:02.167 --> 00:02:04.400
And that's -- So, that's how
I know Greta, yeah.

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:07.801
-Wow! And you told me
that you loved the script.

00:02:07.801 --> 00:02:10.434
-I loved -- Oh, it's one of the
greatest things I've ever read.

00:02:10.434 --> 00:02:12.534
It's going to be --
[ Clicks tongue ]

00:02:12.534 --> 00:02:13.701
Just you wait.
-Yeah, just you wait.

00:02:13.701 --> 00:02:15.067
'Enry 'Iggins, just you wait.

00:02:15.067 --> 00:02:16.968
-You -- "Just you wait."

00:02:16.968 --> 00:02:20.400
You filmed your new series,
"Joe vs. Carole," in Australia.

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:23.868
-"Joe vs. Carole."
-Yes, on Peacock, yeah.

00:02:23.868 --> 00:02:25.200
I just want to talk about
Australia for a second,

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:27.601
because, gosh, I always
wanted to go to Australia.

00:02:27.601 --> 00:02:31.167
Not only do I love Australia,
but I love Australians.

00:02:31.167 --> 00:02:32.267
-You've got to go.

00:02:32.267 --> 00:02:34.033
You've got to go.
You go for the people.

00:02:34.033 --> 00:02:35.634
You go for the animals.

00:02:35.634 --> 00:02:37.033
-There are a lot of
scary animals.

00:02:37.033 --> 00:02:38.234
-A lot of scary animals.

00:02:38.234 --> 00:02:42.367
A lot of anodyne animals,
beautiful little animals,

00:02:42.367 --> 00:02:44.801
who don't kill you.

00:02:44.801 --> 00:02:47.367
And I sort of stuck
with those ones.

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:49.667
-Yeah, not the spiders
and the sharks and stuff.

00:02:49.667 --> 00:02:51.000
-There was my first day there.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:54.667
I was walking on the street and
I saw what I thought was

00:02:54.667 --> 00:02:57.167
the most beautiful bird
I've ever seen in my life.

00:02:57.167 --> 00:03:01.000
Like, this gigantic thing
with a beautiful white plumage

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:04.267
and a long, elegant beak
and, like,

00:03:04.267 --> 00:03:06.300
flapping and just walking
on the sidewalk.

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:10.033
And I was like,
"What is this majestic heron

00:03:10.033 --> 00:03:12.167
just loose in the street
that I've encoun--

00:03:12.167 --> 00:03:14.834
Oh, my God,
I've been blessed here.

00:03:14.834 --> 00:03:16.167
This is a sight!"

00:03:16.167 --> 00:03:19.000
And I asked some guy that
I ran into -- I was like,

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:21.567
"What is this gorgeous bird?"

00:03:21.567 --> 00:03:24.267
And he was like,
"Oh, that's a bin chicken."

00:03:24.267 --> 00:03:28.400
And what I learned was that
the ibis is called a bin chicken

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:31.300
because they eat garbage
out of the dumpsters.

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:33.000
And that is their pigeons,

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:36.801
and they have about eight songs
about how much they hate them.

00:03:36.801 --> 00:03:38.033
And, to me, this was, like,

00:03:38.033 --> 00:03:39.200
the most beautiful thing
I've ever seen.

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:40.267
-To them, it's a pigeon.

00:03:40.267 --> 00:03:42.934
-And they were like,
"Oh, the ibis.

00:03:42.934 --> 00:03:45.434
We hate the ibis."

00:03:45.434 --> 00:03:47.567
-What other animals did you see
when you were in Australia?

00:03:47.567 --> 00:03:51.434
-I saw -- I mean, not to brag,
I saw a kangaroo.

00:03:51.434 --> 00:03:53.033
-Yo!
-Okay?

00:03:53.033 --> 00:03:56.267
-Are they in the wild?
No, kangaroos.

00:03:56.267 --> 00:03:58.601
-There's loose wallabies.

00:03:58.601 --> 00:03:59.734
-Really?
-Just loose.

00:03:59.734 --> 00:04:02.100
-Really?
-On the set, just loose.

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:04.367
And I'm like --
I see these wallabies

00:04:04.367 --> 00:04:08.167
and I'm like, "A wallaby!"

00:04:08.167 --> 00:04:11.234
And they were like,
"Yeah, they're there."

00:04:11.834 --> 00:04:13.167
-"They're there."
-"That's a wallaby."

00:04:13.167 --> 00:04:14.601
-"They're there."
-"So what?"

00:04:14.601 --> 00:04:15.901
-Did you pick up slang?

00:04:15.901 --> 00:04:17.067
Australian -- did you pick up
the accent?

00:04:17.067 --> 00:04:19.734
-I picked --
There's a lot of great slang.

00:04:19.734 --> 00:04:22.634
Everything is abbreviated.
Everything is abbreviated.

00:04:22.634 --> 00:04:25.067
So, sunglasses become sunnies.

00:04:25.067 --> 00:04:26.501
Mosquitoes become mozzies.

00:04:26.501 --> 00:04:30.033
But the best thing I heard was,
the gal who was

00:04:30.033 --> 00:04:33.133
doing my makeup --
Hi, Cath, hi, Iris, hi, Brie.

00:04:33.133 --> 00:04:37.167
Mwah! She said
she needed to scoot

00:04:37.167 --> 00:04:38.701
the wig down just a little bit.

00:04:38.701 --> 00:04:42.267
So she said, "Okay, we're just
going to move it a bee's dick."

00:04:43.033 --> 00:04:46.400
And I was like, "Say again?"

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:47.400
[ Rimshot ]
Thank you.

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:48.968
-That's actually very good.

00:04:48.968 --> 00:04:51.334
-Which is just the smallest
length of distance

00:04:51.334 --> 00:04:52.701
that you could imagine.

00:04:52.701 --> 00:04:54.801
-I've never heard that.
-Just the smallest little bit.

00:04:54.801 --> 00:04:57.334
And come to learn,
that's not an Australian thing.

00:04:57.334 --> 00:04:59.467
That's just her.
-Oh, okay. Oh, interesting.

00:04:59.467 --> 00:05:01.000
Wow. It's good to know
that, yeah.

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:02.334
-She's just that good.

00:05:02.334 --> 00:05:05.968
-Well, the series is
based on the podcast.

00:05:05.968 --> 00:05:08.734
You were working this
before I saw "Tiger King."

00:05:08.734 --> 00:05:11.133
-Yes. This amazing podcast
came out,

00:05:11.133 --> 00:05:13.501
and I listened to it
and I was like,

00:05:13.501 --> 00:05:15.567
"Oh, my gosh, this
Carole Baskin -- what a kook."

00:05:15.567 --> 00:05:17.067
I love kooks.
I love kooky ladies.

00:05:17.067 --> 00:05:18.934
I'm always on the hunt.
-Yeah.

00:05:18.934 --> 00:05:20.767
-And then
the documentary came out,

00:05:20.767 --> 00:05:23.968
and I felt like
she didn't really --

00:05:23.968 --> 00:05:25.434
People didn't
walk away with, like,

00:05:25.434 --> 00:05:28.033
the most rounded picture of
who she is, what she's about,

00:05:28.033 --> 00:05:29.167
and what she's been through.

00:05:29.167 --> 00:05:31.501
She's had quite a tough life.

00:05:31.501 --> 00:05:37.534
And, you know, her main thing --
her main thing -- is, like,

00:05:37.534 --> 00:05:40.667
trying to end
private ownership of big cats

00:05:40.667 --> 00:05:41.868
in the United States.

00:05:41.868 --> 00:05:43.501
Because I don't know if
you guys know this.

00:05:43.501 --> 00:05:47.567
There are currently more tigers
living in cages in captivity

00:05:47.567 --> 00:05:49.234
in the United States
than there are

00:05:49.234 --> 00:05:50.501
in the wild in the whole world.

00:05:50.501 --> 00:05:51.734
-Is that right?

00:05:51.734 --> 00:05:54.601
-And it's just like,
you know, we revere these.

00:05:54.601 --> 00:05:56.000
These are majestic animals.

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:57.868
You wouldn't do that
to something you revere.

00:05:57.868 --> 00:06:02.767
You wouldn't put Olivia Rodrigo
in, you know,

00:06:02.767 --> 00:06:04.133
a cage in your backyard.

00:06:04.133 --> 00:06:06.834
So it just makes no sense.
-She's a national treasure.

00:06:06.834 --> 00:06:07.968
We would never do that to
Olivia Rodrigo.

00:06:07.968 --> 00:06:11.868
-She's a national treasure.
-Of course.

00:06:11.868 --> 00:06:13.501
That's a great example.
Thank you.

00:06:13.501 --> 00:06:15.467
That's a great --
-I know. That's what I'm saying.

00:06:15.467 --> 00:06:16.634
So, you know, it's equivalent.

00:06:16.634 --> 00:06:18.434
And, so,
that's her life's mission.

00:06:18.434 --> 00:06:19.868
And I thought, "Well, you know,

00:06:19.868 --> 00:06:21.901
she deserves some
reconsideration."

00:06:21.901 --> 00:06:23.067
-That's interesting.
-You know?

00:06:23.067 --> 00:06:25.834
-Did you get to know her at all?
Did you meet her?

00:06:25.834 --> 00:06:28.634
-I haven't met her, but she's
done this amazing project

00:06:28.634 --> 00:06:31.567
of putting her entire life story
on YouTube every day

00:06:31.567 --> 00:06:32.901
for the last two years.

00:06:32.901 --> 00:06:34.534
And I watched that and I feel
like I know her and --

00:06:34.534 --> 00:06:35.767
-Yeah, exactly, yeah.

00:06:35.767 --> 00:06:38.067
-And I got more of
a sense of what she's about.

00:06:38.067 --> 00:06:40.968
She's an introvert
and a workaholic and --

00:06:40.968 --> 00:06:42.801
-Okay. Yeah, hello.

00:06:42.801 --> 00:06:45.701
I like that you've found
this new take on her.

00:06:45.701 --> 00:06:47.434
I think it's really cool
that you did that.

00:06:47.434 --> 00:06:48.534
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:06:48.534 --> 00:06:50.367
Here's Kate McKinnon in
"Joe vs. Carole."

00:06:50.367 --> 00:06:51.801
Take a look.

00:06:51.801 --> 00:06:54.868
-What they're counting on is
you getting tired of fighting.

00:06:55.167 --> 00:06:56.167
Yeah.

00:06:57.534 --> 00:07:00.067
Tiger in the wild can't take
a day off, though, right?

00:07:00.067 --> 00:07:01.400
-No.
-No.

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:04.734
-Tiger in the wild can't go to
the pool and read a book.

00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:07.968
Tiger in the wild's
got to be...

00:07:07.968 --> 00:07:10.634
[ Clicks tongue ]
...laser-focused.

00:07:10.634 --> 00:07:12.133
His whole life is a fight.

00:07:12.133 --> 00:07:16.067
So I don't know.

00:07:16.067 --> 00:07:20.033
You want to take a day off
or you want to be a tiger?

00:07:20.033 --> 00:07:21.167
-Be a tiger.
-Tiger.

00:07:21.167 --> 00:07:22.167
-Tiger.
-Yeah.

00:07:22.167 --> 00:07:25.200
-I thought so.

00:07:25.200 --> 00:07:28.801
-Yeah! Let's be a tiger.
Kate McKinnon, everybody!

00:07:28.801 --> 00:07:32.133
"Joe vs. Carole" premieres this
Thursday on Peacock.

